{"_meta":{"securitySchemes":[{"scopes":["openid","profile","email"],"type":"oauth2"}]},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"Get the user a dedicated IP for sites that need one"},"description":"Some sites (LinkedIn, marked 📍 in `get_library`) only accept a login from the address it signed in from. A dedicated IP is one address that only this account uses, and once the account holds one, every sign-in link and every later call on that login uses it automatically.

Call with no arguments first. If the account already holds one, it says so and nothing is bought. Otherwise it returns `priceCents` and a `message` with the price for `termDays` days in `country` (default US). The price is charged up front and is not refundable. If something must happen first (a card on file, a one-time identity check), `mustFirst` names it with the link that fixes it: give your user that link and stop.

**Never buy without asking.** Tell your user the exact price and buy only if they agree, by calling again with `confirmPriceCents` set to the price they agreed to. A live price above that is refused before any charge, and repeating the same call cannot buy two. Pass `another: true` only when your user asked for a second IP.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"another":{"description":"Buy a second IP although the account holds one. Only when your user asked.","type":"boolean"},"confirmPriceCents":{"description":"The price in US cents your user agreed to, from the unconfirmed call. Only this buys.","minimum":0,"type":"number"},"country":{"description":"Two-letter country code for the IP, e.g. "US" (the default).","type":"string"},"termDays":{"description":"How many days the IP is held, paid up front (default 30).","exclusiveMinimum":0,"type":"number"}},"type":"object"},"name":"lease_ip","title":"Get the user a dedicated IP for sites that need one"}

{"_meta":{"securitySchemes":[{"scopes":["openid","profile","email"],"type":"oauth2"}]},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"See which sites Bowmark is already signed in to"},"description":"List the saved logins this account already holds, one entry per login: its `id` (name it in a signed-in call as `{ connection: id }`), the site, which account on that site, whether it works right now (`usable`), and when it was made, last used and last checked.

**Call this before any task that needs a login, and again whenever you come back to one later.** A `usable` login means the site is already signed in: do not ask the user to sign in, just run the script, naming the id if the site has more than one. Prefer the login you used before over a new one.

A login marked `needs_reauth`, `expired` or `logged_out` is not lost. Run the script anyway (name the id if you know it): it pauses with a link, and signing in through that link puts the fresh session back into the SAME id, so you can keep using it. To add a login for a site with none, call `add_connection` — it hands you a sign-in link for the user. `delete_connection` only asks the user to delete one this account already holds.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"properties":{},"type":"object"},"name":"list_connections","title":"See which sites Bowmark is already signed in to"}

{"_meta":{"securitySchemes":[{"scopes":["openid","profile","email"],"type":"oauth2"}]},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":true,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"Call one Bowmark function in a session that keeps its browser"},"description":"Runs ONE library function in a Bowmark session, so a flow that needs several calls in the SAME browser can finish: a booking that texts the user a code, a cart filled over several steps, a form that waits on an answer from the user. `run` cannot do these, because every run starts a fresh browser and the held page dies with it.

`path` is the function as a script writes it after `bowmark.`, split on the dots: `["providers","opentable","startBooking"]`. `args` are its arguments, in order. Look both up in `get_library` first. Omit `sessionId` on the first call: a session opens and its `sessionId` comes back. Pass that `sessionId` on every later call so it runs in the same browser.

The answer is `{ sessionId, ok, status, result, logs, error?, code? }`. `status` is `ok`, `error` or `needs_user`. `needs_user` pauses only this call for a sign-in and the session stays open: give the user `meta.handoff.url`, then repeat the call. A session closes itself after a few idle minutes, so ask the user for anything you need (a texted code) right away and make the next call as soon as they answer. Call `session_close` when the task is done.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"args":{"description":"The function's arguments, in order, exactly as a script passes them.","items":{},"type":"array"},"path":{"description":"The function to call, as the path a script writes after `bowmark.`: `["providers","opentable","startBooking"]` for `bowmark.providers.opentable.startBooking`.","items":{"type":"string"},"minItems":2,"type":"array"},"sessionId":{"description":"The `sessionId` an earlier `session_call` returned. Omit it on the first call and a new session opens.","format":"uuid","type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"},"name":"session_call","title":"Call one Bowmark function in a session that keeps its browser"}

